 "related": [{"id": "objective-c", "relation": "family"}, {"id": "llvm-ir", "relation": "compiles-to"}],
 "level_notes": {"0": "The Swift compiler (swiftlang/swift: C++ front end, SIL optimizer, LLVM-based IRGen) plus its standard library and runtime written in Swift/C++ is the reference implementation. swift-syntax is a second, Swift-written parser used by macros and tooling; Foundation, SwiftPM and SourceKit-LSP live in sibling repositories.", "1": "No ISO/ECMA standard. 'The Swift Programming Language' (TSPL) Language Reference with its grammar summary is the normative-in-practice reference; accepted Swift Evolution proposals define individual features. docs.swift.org (DocC) renders section ids with JavaScript, so #fragments on TSPL pages were verified against the DocC JSON data rather than the static HTML.", "2": "TSPL's Language Guide part is a tutorial (level 2). Slava Pestov's 'Compiling Swift Generics' and the compiler's docs/ folder are internals guides."},
